A museum turnstile counts down and prints the gate number as it goes. What does the program print when turnstile(3) is called? Answers omit the trailing space.
```java
static void turnstile(int n) {
    if (n == 0) return;
    System.out.print(n + " ");
    turnstile(n - 1);
}
```

The same turnstile idea, except the print now sits below the recursive call. What does the program print when turnstile(3) is called? Answers omit the trailing space.
```java
static void turnstile(int n) {
    if (n == 0) return;
    turnstile(n - 1);
    System.out.print(n + " ");
}
```

A tide gauge prints the level on the way down and the negated level on the way back. What does the program print when gauge(2) is called?
```java
static void gauge(int n) {
    if (n == 0) return;
    System.out.print(n + " ");
    gauge(n - 1);
    System.out.print(-n + " ");
}
```

A surveyor labels a patch and then visits both of its halves at every level. What does the program print when branch(3) is called?
```java
static void branch(int n) {
    if (n == 0) return;
    System.out.print(n + " ");
    branch(n - 1);
    branch(n - 1);
}
```

A donation total is carried in a parameter instead of being added up on the way back. What does the call climb(4, 1) return?
```java
static int climb(int n, int acc) {
    if (n == 0) return acc;
    return climb(n - 1, acc + n);
}
```

A packaging line folds its step sizes into a running product instead of a running total. What does the call product(5, 1) return?
```java
static int product(int n, int acc) {
    if (n == 0) return acc;
    return product(n - 1, acc * n);
}
```

A survey keeps the shortest measurement seen so far in a parameter. What does smallest(new int[]{7, 3, 9, 2}, 0, Integer.MAX_VALUE) return?
```java
static int smallest(int[] a, int i, int best) {
    if (i == a.length) return best;
    return smallest(a, i + 1, Math.min(best, a[i]));
}
```

A depth log keeps the deepest reading seen so far in a parameter. What does largest(new int[]{-4, -9, -2}, 0, Integer.MIN_VALUE) return?
```java
static int largest(int[] a, int i, int best) {
    if (i == a.length) return best;
    return largest(a, i + 1, Math.max(best, a[i]));
}
```

A label printer turns a short code around. What does the call flip("cat") return?
```java
static String flip(String s) {
    if (s.length() <= 1) return s;
    return flip(s.substring(1)) + s.charAt(0);
}
```

The same label printer rewritten with an accumulator. What does the call flip("quilt", "") return?
```java
static String flip(String s, String acc) {
    if (s.isEmpty()) return acc;
    return flip(s.substring(1), s.charAt(0) + acc);
}
```

A serial number is rebuilt one digit at a time from the right. What does the call digits(9087, "") return?
```java
static String digits(int n, String acc) {
    if (n < 10) return "" + n + acc;
    return digits(n / 10, (char) ('0' + n % 10) + acc);
}
```

A display buffer is filled after the recursive call returns. What does the program print?
```java
StringBuilder out = new StringBuilder();
write(4087, out);
System.out.println(out);

static void write(int n, StringBuilder out) {
    if (n == 0) return;
    write(n / 10, out);
    out.append(n % 10);
}
```

A reservoir map marks and reports every open cell it can reach from the top left. What does the program print?
```java
int[][] g = { {0, 0, 1}, {0, 0, 0}, {1, 0, 0} };
flood(g, 0, 0, 0);

static void flood(int[][] g, int r, int c, int fill) {
    if (r < 0 || c < 0 || r >= g.length || c >= g[0].length) return;
    if (g[r][c] != fill) return;
    g[r][c] = -1;
    System.out.print("(" + r + "," + c + ")");
    flood(g, r + 1, c, fill);
    flood(g, r - 1, c, fill);
    flood(g, r, c + 1, fill);
    flood(g, r, c - 1, fill);
}
```

A courier walks open cells to the right first and then downward, marking each one as it goes. What does the program print?
```java
int[][] g = { {0, 0, 0}, {0, 1, 0}, {0, 0, 0} };
walk(g, 0, 0);

static void walk(int[][] g, int r, int c) {
    if (r < 0 || c < 0 || r >= g.length || c >= g[0].length) return;
    if (g[r][c] != 0) return;
    g[r][c] = 1;
    System.out.print(r + "" + c + " ");
    walk(g, r, c + 1);
    walk(g, r + 1, c);
}
```

A table dump separates each finished row with a bar. What does the program print?
```java
int[][] g = { {1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6} };
rows(g, 0, 0);

static void rows(int[][] g, int r, int c) {
    if (r >= g.length) return;
    if (c < g[0].length) { System.out.print(g[r][c] + " "); rows(g, r, c + 1); }
    else { System.out.print("|"); rows(g, r + 1, 0); }
}
```

A batch of readings hangs off a linked chain 4 to 1 to 7 to 3. What does the program print, ignoring the returned total?
```java
static int total(Node p) {
    if (p == null) return 0;
    int sub = total(p.next);
    System.out.print(p.v + " ");
    return p.v + sub;
}
```

A stack of parcels is dumped from the top down a linked chain 2 to 9 to 5 to 6 to 1. What does the program print?
```java
static void back(Node p) {
    if (p == null) return;
    back(p.next);
    System.out.print(p.v + " ");
}
```

A quality check tallies the readings above three on the chain 4 to 1 to 7 to 3. What does the call countBig(head) return?
```java
static int countBig(Node p) {
    if (p == null) return 0;
    return (p.v > 3 ? 1 : 0) + countBig(p.next);
}
```

Three nodes are linked 1 to 2 to 3, and node three points back at node two. What does the call tour(head) return when each node carries a seen flag that starts false?
```java
static int tour(Node p) {
    if (p == null) return 0;
    if (p.seen) return 0;
    p.seen = true;
    return 1 + tour(p.next);
}
```

A locker check reports whether any stored value is even. How many times does the line that tests for an even value run when hasEven(new int[]{1, 3, 6, 2}, 0) is called?
```java
static boolean hasEven(int[] a, int i) {
    if (i == a.length) return false;
    if (a[i] % 2 == 0) return true;
    return hasEven(a, i + 1);
}
```

A manifest check reports whether every entry is above the floor. How many times does the line that tests for a negative entry run when allPositive(new int[]{2, -1, 5, 7}, 0) is called?
```java
static boolean allPositive(int[] a, int i) {
    if (i == a.length) return true;
    if (a[i] < 0) return false;
    return allPositive(a, i + 1);
}
```

Parity is split across two methods that hand the argument back and forth. How many times is one of the two bodies entered when isEven(5) is called?
```java
static boolean isEven(int n) {
    if (n == 0) return true;
    return isOdd(n - 1);
}
static boolean isOdd(int n) {
    if (n == 0) return false;
    return isEven(n - 1);
}
```

Two methods label a countdown and hand the smaller argument to each other. What does the program print when down(3) is called?
```java
static void down(int n) {
    if (n <= 0) return;
    System.out.print("d" + n + " ");
    up(n - 1);
}
static void up(int n) {
    if (n <= 0) return;
    System.out.print("u" + n + " ");
    down(n - 1);
}
```

A ladder total is reported as each level unrolls. What does the program print when total(4) is called?
```java
static int total(int n) {
    if (n == 0) return 0;
    int sub = total(n - 1);
    System.out.print(n + " ");
    return n + sub;
}
```

Two shapes compute the same total, and a driver resets the counters and reports the peak depth after each run. What two values does the driver print?
```java
static int depth = 0;
static int peak = 0;

static int head(int n) {
    if (n == 0) return 0;
    depth++;
    if (depth > peak) peak = depth;
    int r = n + head(n - 1);
    depth--;
    return r;
}

static int tail(int n, int acc) {
    if (n == 0) return acc;
    depth++;
    if (depth > peak) peak = depth;
    int r = tail(n - 1, acc + n);
    depth--;
    return r;
}

// driver: peak = 0; depth = 0; head(5);  System.out.println(peak);
//         peak = 0; depth = 0; tail(5, 0); System.out.println(peak);
```

A frame printer draws a shrinking frame at each level and then descends. What does the program print when frame(3) is called?
```java
static void frame(int n) {
    if (n == 0) return;
    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) System.out.print(i);
    System.out.print("|");
    frame(n - 1);
}
```

A chute printer was supposed to stop at zero but the guard was lost in a merge. What happens when down(3) is called?
```java
static void down(int n) {
    System.out.print(n + " ");
    down(n - 1);
}
```

A step counter was meant to walk down to zero but the arrow was reversed in one place. What happens when climb(1) is called?
```java
static int climb(int n) {
    if (n <= 0) return 0;
    return 1 + climb(n + 1);
}
```

A packaging count used to multiply its step sizes and now always reports nothing packaged. What does the call fact(5, 0) return, and what is the defect?
```java
static int fact(int n, int acc) {
    if (n == 0) return acc;
    return fact(n - 1, acc * n);
}
```

A crate label was supposed to be turned around. What does the call flip("quilt", "") return, and what is the defect?
```java
static String flip(String s, String acc) {
    if (s.isEmpty()) return acc;
    return flip(s.substring(1), acc + s.charAt(0));
}
```

A flood guard was shortened to save a line and the walk now dies on its second step. What happens when slide(g, 0, 0) is called on int[][] g = { {0, 0, 0}, {0, 1, 0} }?
```java
static void slide(int[][] g, int r, int c) {
    if (r >= g.length || c >= g[0].length) return;
    if (g[r][c] == 1) return;
    g[r][c] = 1;
    System.out.print(r + "" + c + " ");
    slide(g, r - 1, c);
    slide(g, r, c - 1);
}
```

A manifest check is supposed to report whether an array holds no negative entries, but it says yes to everything. Which single line replaces the second return so the method becomes correct?
```java
static boolean noNegatives(int[] a, int i) {
    if (i == a.length) return true;
    if (a[i] < 0) return true;
    return noNegatives(a, i + 1);
}
```

A serial display shows its digits in the wrong order. What does the builder hold after write(4087, out) runs, and what is the defect?
```java
static void write(int n, StringBuilder out) {
    if (n == 0) return;
    out.append(n % 10);
    write(n / 10, out);
}
```

A counter was meant to return the number of entries in a list of length n but now returns too many. What does count(8) return, and what is the defect?
```java
static int count(int n) {
    if (n <= 1) return 1;
    return 1 + count(n / 2) + count(n / 2);
}
```

A search halves the number it is looking in and pays one unit of work per level. How many times is the body entered when steps(1000) is called?
```java
static int steps(int n) {
    if (n <= 1) return 0;
    return steps(n / 2) + 1;
}
```

A divide-and-conquer step splits the range into two halves and pays one unit at every entry. How many times is the body entered when work(8) is called?
```java
static int work(int n) {
    if (n <= 1) return 0;
    return work(n / 2) + work(n - n / 2) + 1;
}
```

A survey body walks the same smaller problem twice at every level and does nothing else. How many times is the body entered when cost(5) is called?
```java
static int cost(int n) {
    if (n == 0) return 0;
    cost(n - 1);
    cost(n - 1);
    return 1;
}
```

A six-letter word is reversed with a shape that joins text at every level. How many times does the join run when flip("puzzle") is called?
```java
static String flip(String s) {
    if (s.length() <= 1) return s;
    return flip(s.substring(1)) + s.charAt(0);
}
```
